Subject: gemma4uv: budget-fill image preprocessing + F32 projector accumulation

Port of chippydip/llama.cpp gemma4uv-vision-fix (db40e8c5) onto our pin.

The unified Gemma 4 vision path was using smart_resize semantics (keep
image size when within min/max token bounds), but the reference
Gemma4UnifiedImageProcessor.get_aspect_ratio_preserving_size ALWAYS
rescales (up or down) so the image fills the soft-token budget
(max_soft_tokens=280 -> 768x768 for square inputs). The model never saw
small patch grids in training; feeding it a 49-token image produces
garbled perception ("cropped/zoomed" confabulation, text read as
per-patch slivers). Upstream's 40-token minimum was a partial mitigation
of the same issue.

- new mtmd_image_preprocessor_gemma4: aspect-preserving budget-fill
  resize (floor each side to a multiple of the 48px patch), BICUBIC
  (reference uses bicubic+antialias; bilinear loses text detail),
  direct resize without padding
- gemma4uv graph: force F32 accumulation on the patch-embedding and
  final projection matmuls (F16 accumulation overflows on high-contrast
  patches -> Inf/NaN on CUDA-class backends; upstream issue #24251)

Note: image token count for typical inputs rises to ~256, so chat and
(CPU-only) media-embedding requests carry longer prompts.
